message.content:
This is aluminum foil tape, self-adhesive, in rolls. Two headings are candidates: 3919 (self-adhesive plates, sheets, film, foil, tape, strip of plastics) and 7607 (aluminum foil, backed or not).

Heading 3919 covers plastics articles only, so it does not fit an aluminum foil tape. Heading 7607 covers aluminum foil (whether or not printed or backed with paper, paperboard, plastics or similar backing) with a thickness not exceeding 0.2 mm excluding backing. Self-adhesive aluminum foil tape is generally classified in 7607.19 (not backed, other). Subheading 7607.11 covers rolled but not further worked, while 7607.19 covers other. Coating with adhesive is further working, so 7607.19. Subheadings 7607.19.10 (not cut to shape, thickness under 0.15 mm, ...) and 7607.19.30 and 7607.19.60 are the candidates. The stat suffix 7607.19.1000 is "Not cut to shape" and I recall 7607.19.1000 covers foil of a thickness not exceeding 0.15 mm... Actually, the HTS has 7607.19.10 "Not cut to shape" with 7607.19.1000 and 7607.19.30 "Other: Cut to shape", and 7607.19.60 "Other". Customs rulings on adhesive aluminum foil tape, such as in the antidumping case on aluminum foil, have used 7607.19.6000. The scope of aluminum foil tape cases (self-wound) mentions 7607.19.6000, among others. I will go with 7607.19.6000.

{"hts_code": "7607.19.6000", "reason": "Adhesive-coated aluminum foil under 0.2 mm thick without a backing is aluminum foil of heading 7607, further worked than merely rolled, so it falls in the 'other' subheading 7607.19.60."}
